{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1792266495103,"sessionID":"ses_eb497bcceffeROWha5Uz0kLbec","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"webfetch","callID":"call_vjnget99va5uy8urlz2c7hr1","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2410.10135"},"output":" \\[2410.10135\\] FormalAlign: Automated Alignment Evaluation for Autoformalization                               \n\n[Skip to main content](#content)\n\n[](https://arxiv.org/IgnoreMe)[![archive](/static/base/1.0.1/images/arxiv-logo-primary-light.svg)](https://arxiv.org/)\n\n[Search](https://arxiv.org/search) [Submit](https://arxiv.org/user/create) [Donate](https://info.arxiv.org/about/donate.html) [Log in](https://arxiv.org/login)\n\nSearch arXiv   \n\nPress Enter to search · [Advanced search](https://arxiv.org/search/advanced)\n\n# Computer Science > Computation and Language\n\n**arXiv:2410.10135** (cs)\n\n\\[Submitted on 14 Oct 2024\\]\n\n# Title:FormalAlign: Automated Alignment Evaluation for Autoformalization\n\nAuthors:[Jianqiao Lu](https://arxiv.org/search/cs?searchtype=author&query=Lu,+J), [Yingjia Wan](https://arxiv.org/search/cs?searchtype=author&query=Wan,+Y), [Yinya Huang](https://arxiv.org/search/cs?searchtype=author&query=Huang,+Y), [Jing Xiong](https://arxiv.org/search/cs?searchtype=author&query=Xiong,+J), [Zhengying Liu](https://arxiv.org/search/cs?searchtype=author&query=Liu,+Z), [Zhijiang Guo](https://arxiv.org/search/cs?searchtype=author&query=Guo,+Z)\n\nView a PDF of the paper titled FormalAlign: Automated Alignment Evaluation for Autoformalization, by Jianqiao Lu and 5 other authors\n\n[View PDF](/pdf/2410.10135) [HTML (experimental)](https://arxiv.org/html/2410.10135v1)\n\n> Abstract:Autoformalization aims to convert informal mathematical proofs into machine-verifiable formats, bridging the gap between natural and formal languages. However, ensuring semantic alignment between the informal and formalized statements remains challenging. Existing approaches heavily rely on manual verification, hindering scalability. To address this, we introduce \\\\textsc{FormalAlign}, the first automated framework designed for evaluating the alignment between natural and formal languages in autoformalization. \\\\textsc{FormalAlign} trains on both the autoformalization sequence generation task and the representational alignment between input and output, employing a dual loss that combines a pair of mutually enhancing autoformalization and alignment tasks. Evaluated across four benchmarks augmented by our proposed misalignment strategies, \\\\textsc{FormalAlign} demonstrates superior performance. In our experiments, \\\\textsc{FormalAlign} outperforms GPT-4, achieving an Alignment-Selection Score 11.58\\\\% higher on \\\\forml-Basic (99.21\\\\% vs. 88.91\\\\%) and 3.19\\\\% higher on MiniF2F-Valid (66.39\\\\% vs. 64.34\\\\%). This effective alignment evaluation significantly reduces the need for manual verification. Both the dataset and code can be accessed via~\\\\url{[this https URL](https://github.com/rookie-joe/FormalAlign)}.\n\nComments:\n\n23 pages, 13 tables, 3 figures\n\nSubjects:\n\nComputation and Language (cs.CL); Artificial Intelligence (cs.AI); Formal Languages and Automata Theory (cs.FL); Machine Learning (cs.LG)\n\nCite as:\n\n[arXiv:2410.10135](https://arxiv.org/abs/2410.10135) \\[cs.CL\\]\n\n \n\n(or [arXiv:2410.10135v1](https://arxiv.org/abs/2410.10135v1) \\[cs.CL\\] for this version)\n\n \n\n[https://doi.org/10.48550/arXiv.2410.10135](https://doi.org/10.48550/arXiv.2410.10135)\n\nFocus to learn more\n\narXiv-issued DOI via DataCite\n\n## Submission history\n\nFrom: Jianqiao Lu \\[[view email](/show-email/d5505deb/2410.10135)\\]  \n**\\[v1\\]** Mon, 14 Oct 2024 03:58:35 UTC (1,250 KB)  \n\nFull-text links:\n\n## Access Paper:\n\nView a PDF of the paper titled FormalAlign: Automated Alignment Evaluation for Autoformalization, by Jianqiao Lu and 5 other authors\n\n-   [View PDF](/pdf/2410.10135)\n-   [HTML (experimental)](https://arxiv.org/html/2410.10135v1)\n-   [TeX Source](/src/2410.10135)\n\n [![license icon](https://arxiv.org/icons/licenses/by-4.0.png) view license](http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/ \"Rights to this article\")\n\n### Current browse context:\n\ncs.CL\n\n[< prev](/prevnext?id=2410.10135&function=prev&context=cs.CL \"previous in cs.CL (accesskey p)\")   |   [next >](/prevnext?id=2410.10135&function=next&context=cs.CL \"next in cs.CL (accesskey n)\")  \n\n[new](/list/cs.CL/new) | [recent](/list/cs.CL/recent) | [2024-10](/list/cs.CL/2024-10)\n\nChange to browse by:\n\n[cs](/abs/2410.10135?context=cs)  \n[cs.AI](/abs/2410.10135?context=cs.AI)  \n[cs.FL](/abs/2410.10135?context=cs.FL)  \n[cs.LG](/abs/2410.10135?context=cs.LG)  \n\n### References & Citations\n\n-   [NASA ADS](https://ui.adsabs.harvard.edu/abs/arXiv:2410.10135)\n-   [Google Scholar](https://scholar.google.com/scholar_lookup?arxiv_id=2410.10135)\n-   [Semantic Scholar](https://api.semanticscholar.org/arXiv:2410.10135)\n\nexport BibTeX citation Loading...\n\n## BibTeX formatted citation\n\n×\n\nloading...\n\nData provided by:\n\n### Bookmark\n\n [![BibSonomy](/static/browse/0.3.4/images/icons/social/bibsonomy.png)](http://www.bibsonomy.org/BibtexHandler?requTask=upload&url=https://arxiv.org/abs/2410.10135&description=FormalAlign: Automated Alignment Evaluation for Autoformalization \"Bookmark on BibSonomy\")[![Reddit](/static/browse/0.3.4/images/icons/social/reddit.png)](https://reddit.com/submit?url=https://arxiv.org/abs/2410.10135&title=FormalAlign: Automated Alignment Evaluation for Autoformalization \"Bookmark on Reddit\")\n\n Bibliographic Tools\n\n# Bibliographic and Citation Tools\n\n Bibliographic Explorer Toggle\n\nBibliographic Explorer *([What is the Explorer?](https://info.arxiv.org/labs/showcase.html#arxiv-bibliographic-explorer))*\n\n Connected Papers Toggle\n\nConnected Papers *([What is Connected Papers?](https://www.connectedpapers.com/about))*\n\n Litmaps Toggle\n\nLitmaps *([What is Litmaps?](https://www.l