{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1792266566905,"sessionID":"ses_eb497bcceffeROWha5Uz0kLbec","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"websearch","callID":"call_902d08dup4u8oz6jcc84umg4","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"query":"Kimina-Prover \"repeatedly make mistakes that the LLM judge model cannot catch\" compilation"},"output":"Title: Kimina-Prover Preview: Towards Large Formal Reasoning Models with Reinforcement Learning\nURL: https://arxiv.org/html/2504.11354\nPublished: 2025-04-15T00:00:00.000Z\nAuthor: Numina, Kimi Team\nHighlights:\nWe note that this method required careful expert monitoring as we observe that the model would repeatedly make mistakes that the LLM judge model cannot catch, as long as it passed compilation. We believe this presents a significant challenge in applying reinforcement learning in non-verifiable domains.\n\n---\n\nTitle: Following the supervised fine-tuning (SFT) phase, we employ reinforcement learning (RL) to further enhance our model’s formal theorem-proving capabilities, as illustrated in the pipeline schematic (Figure 2). The RL process iteratively refines the model’s policy. Each iteration begins by sampling a batch of\n𝑁\nURL: https://d6108366.hf-mirror.com/papers/2504.11354\nPublished: N/A\nAuthor: N/A\nHighlights:\nWe note that this method required careful expert monitoring as we observe that the model would repeatedly make mistakes that the LLM judge model cannot catch, as long as it passed compilation. We believe this presents a significant challenge in applying reinforcement learning in non-verifiable domains.\n\n---\n\nTitle: Kimina-Prover Preview: Towards Large Formal Reasoning Models with Reinforcement Learning\nURL: https://arxiv.org/html/2504.11354v1\nPublished: 2025-04-15T00:00:00.000Z\nAuthor: Numina, Kimi Team\nHighlights:\nWe note that this method required careful expert monitoring as we observe that the model would repeatedly make mistakes that the LLM judge model cannot catch, as long as it passed compilation. We beli